Imagine you are building a system that reads data from different file types
like CSV , XML and JSON
every reader has -> open the file , read the content , close the file

if we don't use template pattern , we will end up writing the same opening and closing logic over and
over again in each file reader class


Basically open() and close() can be called as templates
and the parse() -> plugin which varies between the type

Problems:
Repeated Code
Hard to Maintain -> if you want to modify logic of open and file , you modify every everywhere
It violates
DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)


Create AbstractClass
template() -> Template Method : open() parse() close()  -> the way how template for parse is done
open()
close()
parse() -> abstract method -> change for each file type class

CSVParser -----|> Data (Inherit)